\noindent \emph{Figure }\emph{31}\emph{.} Results (Part 1) of a Full All-Invariant CoTiMA with Six Studies (\code{ctmaFit})

Similarly, \code{DIFFUSIONcov} are the continuous time error variances (usually referred to as diffusion term in the literature), and \code{asymDIFFUSIONcov} reflect asymptotic diffusion (error) variances and covariances. One might speculate that the asymptotic diffusion (error) variances should be 1.0 since one cannot explain any variance across infinite time. However, these estimates are based on internal transformations, which are internally useful to reduce the time to fit the model but have no inherent meaning.

\code{MANIFESTcov} is a matrix of variances and covariances among the manifest variables at each measurement occasion. All values were fixed to 0.0 because we had only a single manifest indicator per latent factor.

